1680fb08-eeb8-4d2e-ae74-a5182bcc7ad9	delay	this is for the delay report	file	\N	https://tlczogmizfbjtrbnsrxc.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/reports/2026-05-13/35b88b81-8c2d-4ca3-b60c-95ac0367c3ec-Customer_Credit_Approval_and_New_Customer_Onboarding_Process__1_.docx	Customer Credit Approval and New Customer Onboarding Process (1).docx	application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document	2026-05-13 03:07:04.072226+00	this is for the delay report	df47d5f4-9178-4c9b-8b37-c1a186e752b1	Customer Credit Approval and New Customer Onboarding Process\rDocument Status: Draft (Unstandardized)\vBusiness Unit: DHL Logistics Operations\vProcess Owner: Operations & Finance\vLast Updated: Not maintained consistently\r\r1. Purpose\rThe purpose of this Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) is to document the end-to-end process for new customer onboarding with credit approval in DHL Logistics Operations. This SOP aims to explain how new customers are set up in operational and financial systems, how credit checks are conducted, and how approvals or rejections are handled.\rCurrently, this process is handled through a mix of emails, spreadsheets, informal instructions, and experience-based knowledge. This document consolidates existing practices but has not been fully standardized. The intention is to later refine this SOP into a clean and official knowledge article.\r\r2. Scope\rThis SOP applies to:\r Operations teams\r Customer Service teams\r Finance and Credit Control teams\r Supervisors and Managers involved in customer onboarding\rThis SOP covers:\r New customer request intake\r Credit evaluation and approval\r System setup\r Communication with stakeholders\rIt does not cover customer contract negotiation or legal agreement signing.\r\r3. Definitions and Abbreviations\r CRM – Customer Relationship Management system\r SAP – Enterprise Resource Planning system used for billing and finance\r Credit Limit – Maximum allowed outstanding amount for a customer\r Cash Customer – Customer required to prepay before shipment\r Credit Customer – Customer allowed to ship and pay later based on approved credit terms\r\r4. Roles and Responsibilities\r4.1 Sales Team\r Submit new customer onboarding request\r Provide complete customer information\r Support clarifications during credit review\r4.2 Operations Team\r Validate onboarding request completeness\r Coordinate with Finance for system setup\r Ensure customer is ready for operational use\r4.3 Finance / Credit Control Team\r Perform credit checks\r Approve or reject credit requests\r Set credit terms and limits in SAP\r4.4 Management\r Approve exceptional cases\r Resolve escalations and delays\r\r5. Process Overview\rThe new customer onboarding and credit approval process consists of the following high-level steps:\r1. New customer request received\r2. Initial validation of request\r3. Credit evaluation\r4. Approval or rejection decision\r5. System setup\r6. Confirmation to stakeholders\rDelays frequently occur due to incomplete information, unclear ownership, or delayed approvals.\r\r6. Detailed Process Steps\r\r6.1 New Customer Request Submission\rNew customer onboarding requests are typically initiated by the Sales team. Requests are submitted through email or shared templates. There is no single standardized form currently used across all regions.\rMinimum information required includes:\r Legal company name\r Company registration number\r Billing address\r Operational address (if different)\r Estimated monthly volume\r Requested credit limit\r Requested payment terms (e.g., 30 days)\rSome requests arrive with missing or inconsistent information, which causes delays.\r\r6.2 Initial Validation by Operations\rUpon receiving the request, Operations performs a basic validation to ensure that all required information is provided. This step is usually done manually by checking emails and attachments.\rCommon issues found during this stage:\r Missing registration documents\r Incomplete billing address\r No estimated shipment volume provided\r Unclear payment terms\rWhen information is missing, Operations contacts Sales for clarification. This back-and-forth often happens over multiple emails.\r\r6.3 Credit Evaluation by Finance\rOnce the request is validated, it is forwarded to the Finance or Credit Control team for evaluation. The credit evaluation process may include:\r Internal credit history check (if existing customer in other countries)\r External credit bureau checks\r Assessment of requested credit limit versus shipment volume\r Review of financial documents\rBased on the evaluation, Finance decides whether the customer should be:\r Approved as a credit customer\r Approved with a lower credit limit\r Approved as cash-only\r Rejected\rThis decision-making process is not always documented clearly.\r\r6.4 Approval Scenarios\r6.4.1 Credit Approved as Requested\rIf the credit request is approved:\r Finance confirms the approved credit limit and payment terms\r Details are shared with Operations\r System setup can begin\r6.4.2 Credit Approved with Conditions\rSometimes credit is approved with conditions such as:\r Reduced credit limit\r Shorter payment terms\r Partial prepaid requirement\rThese conditions are communicated via email but not always captured in a structured format.\r6.4.3 Credit Rejected\rIf credit is rejected:\r Customer may be offered cash-only terms\r Sales is informed to manage customer expectations\r Request may be closed or reworked\r\r6.5 System Setup\rAfter credit approval, the Operations and Finance teams proceed with system setup.\rTypical system activities include:\r Creating customer record in CRM\r Creating customer master data in SAP\r Assigning billing and operational roles\r Configuring tax and invoicing parameters\rSystem setup errors are common due to manual data entry.\r\r6.6 Common System Setup Issues\rFrequently observed issues include:\r Duplicate customer records\r Incorrect billing currency\r Wrong tax code assigned\r Credit limit mismatch between email approval and SAP setup\rWhen issues occur, tickets are raised to IT or Finance, causing delays.\r\r6.7 Confirmation to Stakeholders\rOnce setup is completed:\r Operations confirms readiness for shipment processing\r Sales is informed that the customer is live\r Finance monitors the first few invoices closely\rThere is no standardized checklist to confirm all steps are completed before go-live.\r\r7. Exception Handling and Escalations\r7.1 Delayed Credit Approval\rIf credit approval takes more than 5 working days:\r Operations escalates to Finance Manager\r Sales may request temporary cash terms to start operations\r\r7.2 Urgent Customer Go-Live Requests\rIn some cases, urgent onboarding is required. Temporary workarounds include:\r Cash-only setup\r Manual billing\r Later credit conversion\rThese practices increase operational risk.\r\r8. Risks and Known Gaps\rThe following issues have been identified:\r Heavy manual processing\r Lack of standardized forms\r No centralized tracking\r Dependency on email communication\r Limited audit trail\rNew joiners often struggle to understand the process due to lack of clear documentation.\r\r9. Compliance and Audit Considerations\rImproper customer setup can lead to:\r Revenue leakage\r Bad debt exposure\r Compliance violations\r Audit findings\rFinance periodically reviews customer credit exposure, but corrections are reactive rather than preventive.\r\r10. Training and Knowledge Sharing\rCurrently, training is conducted informally through:\r Shadowing experienced staff\r Email instructions\r Chat-based guidance\rThis SOP is intended to evolve into a proper training reference.\r\r11. Summary\rThis SOP documents the current-state process for customer credit approval and onboarding. While it captures real operational practices, it lacks standardization, structure, and automation. The content should be transformed into a cleaner SOP, simplified checklist, and searchable Knowledge Base articles.\r\r	{"title":"Customer Credit Approval and New Customer Onboarding Process","summary_steps":"This is a Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) for new customer onboarding with credit approval in DHL Logistics Operations.","key_points":"• This SOP documents the end-to-end process for new customer onboarding with credit approval in DHL Logistics Operations.\\n• The process is currently handled through a mix of emails, spreadsheets, informal instructions, and experience-based knowledge.\\n• The SOP applies to Operations, Customer Service, Finance, Credit Control teams, Supervisors, and Managers involved in customer onboarding.\\n• The process covers new customer request intake, credit evaluation and approval, system setup, and communication with stakeholders.\\n• Delays frequently occur due to incomplete information, unclear ownership, or delayed approvals.\\n• Identified risks include heavy manual processing, lack of standardized forms, no centralized tracking, and dependency on email communication.","sop":"Document Type / Title\\n• Standard Operating Procedure (SOP)\\n\\nName / Author\\n• Process Owner: Operations & Finance\\n\\nImportant Concepts / Topics\\n• CRM – Customer Relationship Management system\\n• SAP – Enterprise Resource Planning system used for billing and finance\\n• Credit Limit – Maximum allowed outstanding amount for a customer\\n• Cash Customer – Customer required to prepay before shipment\\n• Credit Customer – Customer allowed to ship and pay later based on approved credit terms\\n\\nRequirements / Objectives\\n• Document the end-to-end process for new customer onboarding with credit approval\\n• Explain how new customers are set up in operational and financial systems\\n• Explain how credit checks are conducted\\n• Explain how approvals or rejections are handled\\n\\nOther Relevant Information\\n• Document Status: Draft (Unstandardized)\\n• Business Unit: DHL Logistics Operations\\n• Last Updated: Not maintained consistently\\n• Scope applies to: Operations teams, Customer Service teams, Finance and Credit Control teams, Supervisors and Managers involved in customer onboarding\\n• Scope covers: New customer request intake, Credit evaluation and approval, System setup, Communication with stakeholders\\n• Scope does not cover: customer contract negotiation or legal agreement signing\\n• Roles and Responsibilities: Sales Team, Operations Team, Finance / Credit Control Team, Management\\n• Process Overview: New customer request received, Initial validation of request, Credit evaluation, Approval or rejection decision, System setup, Confirmation to stakeholders\\n• New customer onboarding requests are typically initiated by the Sales team\\n• Minimum information required for requests: Legal company name, Company registration number, Billing address, Operational address, Estimated monthly volume, Requested credit limit, Requested payment terms\\n• Initial Validation by Operations checks for missing registration documents, incomplete billing address, no estimated shipment volume, unclear payment terms\\n• Credit Evaluation by Finance may include: Internal credit history check, External credit bureau checks, Assessment of requested credit limit, Review of financial documents\\n• Approval Scenarios: Credit Approved as Requested, Credit Approved with Conditions, Credit Rejected\\n• System Setup activities include: Creating customer record in CRM, Creating customer master data in SAP, Assigning billing and operational roles, Configuring tax and invoicing parameters\\n• Common System Setup Issues: Duplicate customer records, Incorrect billing currency, Wrong tax code assigned, Credit limit mismatch\\n• Confirmation to Stakeholders: Operations confirms readiness, Sales is informed, Finance monitors first invoices\\n• Exception Handling and Escalations: Delayed Credit Approval (escalate to Finance Manager), Urgent Customer Go-Live Requests (cash-only setup, manual billing)\\n• Risks and Known Gaps: Heavy manual processing, Lack of standardized forms, No centralized tracking, Dependency on email communication, Limited audit trail\\n• Compliance and Audit Considerations: Improper customer setup can lead to revenue leakage, bad debt exposure, compliance violations, audit findings\\n• Training and Knowledge Sharing: Currently conducted informally through shadowing, email instructions, chat-based guidance","v":5}	processed	2026-05-13 03:10:52.689+00	ok i will get in touch with you	urgent	delay	3	The report indicates frequent delays in the customer onboarding process due to incomplete information, impacting operations.	2026-05-13 03:08:48.54+00	[0.0035753322, 0.0096437875, -0.00788824, -0.05408113, 0.0006460471, 0.0038793825, -0.0002552679, 0.0056125955, -0.043748952, 0.014260649, -0.023943843, -0.0003909001, 0.012031941, 0.01671999, 0.09842223, -0.0062765093, 0.0007262897, 0.016814519, -0.015754277, 0.002154909, -0.011200546, 0.0073230425, 0.003224171, -0.00075549626, 0.012648651, -0.0038623698, 0.004909067, 0.010183715, 0.031274613, 0.011364327, 0.0170718, 0.0048144218, 0.0033594747, -0.002841901, 0.005751097, 0.03906546, 0.021397494, 0.000062222556, 0.0017330332, 0.017644564, 0.00007638244, -0.001320019, 0.004710299, -0.018611318, -0.025437737, -0.00050684955, -0.00053910504, -0.041276656, 0.011493688, 0.021377223, -0.009724542, -0.005786451, 0.021707471, -0.16309568, -0.013955278, -0.024540262, -0.0040181065, -0.0047311205, 0.008264072, -0.039702322, -0.023183996, 0.03301458, -0.024444163, -0.030302927, -0.013641642, -0.022575628, 0.0015985102, 0.0091053285, -0.020091968, -0.0015142479, -0.0042652325, -0.0011488891, -0.0059856633, 0.0072048856, -0.02388509, -0.049252354, 0.008245045, 0.000009394588, -0.031141028, 0.0026318193, 0.0017229082, -0.024839334, 0.0062013767, -0.036005475, -0.008794246, 0.005041391, 0.0013542271, 0.0065532704, -0.0041236784, 0.00020700642, -0.006578847, 0.