3d7af321-426a-46ba-a085-87af770c8cf3	resume	muntasirs resume	file	\N	https://tlczogmizfbjtrbnsrxc.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/reports/2026-05-11/d01715a6-9351-410e-95ef-fe50497e4daa-muntaisrsirkhaziresume.pdf	muntaisrsirkhaziresume.pdf	application/pdf	2026-05-11 07:38:51.494551+00	muntasirs resume	df47d5f4-9178-4c9b-8b37-c1a186e752b1	MUNTASIR RAHAMAN SIRKHAZI\r\n\r\nMalaysia, Kuala Lumpur |muntasirrahman23@gmail.com | 010 707 6149|github| Linkedin |\r\n\r\nABOUT MYSELF\r\n\r\nI am a dedicated software engineering student with strong expertise in full-stack development and a proven ability to\r\ndeliver scalable, user-focused solutions. With a solid foundation in programming, database management, and system\r\ndesign, I bring analytical problem-solving skills and a commitment to excellence in every project.\r\n\r\nEDUCATION\r\n\r\n October, 2023 (Malaysia–Japan International Institute of Technology (MJIIT), UNIVERSITY TECHNOLOGY\r\nMALAYSIA) (CURRENT)\r\n\r\nBachelor of Computer Science (Software Engineering) with Honours\r\n\r\n April, 2020 - April, 2021(INTERNATIONAL INDIAN SCHOOL DAMMAM, SAUDI ARABIA)\r\n\r\nSenior Secondary School (STPM/A-Levels Equivalent)\r\n\r\n April, 2018 - April, 2019(INTERNATIONAL INDIAN SCHOOL DAMMAM, SAUDI ARABIA)\r\n\r\nSecondary School (SPM/O-Levels Equivalent)\r\n\r\nHARD SKILL AND LANGUAGES\r\n\r\nSkills- MySQL, php, html, CSS, JAVASCRIPT, python, Java, C++, React js , bootstrap, tailwind css , Assembly Language,\r\nnode.js, nextjs and mongo db.\r\n\r\nTools:- GitHub, Cisco Packet Tracer, postman, Microsoft VScode, Oracle VirtualBox, Geekbench, CPU-Z, mongodb,\r\nTampermonkey\r\n\r\nLanguages- English, Hindi and Urdu\r\n\r\nSoft Skills- Communication, Teamwork, Problem-solving, Adaptability, Time management, Leadership and Creativity\r\n\r\nPROJECTS\r\n\r\nSmart Interview Analyzer: -  https://youtu.be/BHxqY5FBcks\r\n\r\n Built a full-stack asynchronous media analysis platform using React + Tailwind, Node.js (Express), Python, and\r\nPostgreSQL.\r\n Designed REST APIs and background worker architecture to process uploaded audio/video and compute NLP-\r\nbased performance metrics.\r\n Implemented speech analysis pipeline in Python to extract transcript features and generate structured\r\nconfidence scoring.\r\n Developed relational database models to manage job state transitions and analytics persistence\r\n\r\nPayment Tracking System (full stack): - https://youtu.be/8gf2CVAjzGE Developed a full-stack tuition payment management system using Next.js, Tailwind CSS, and Supabase for a\r\nprivate tuition center.\r\n This is a system for sksentul 2 which is a small school located in Malaysia\r\n Implemented role-based access control for parents, teachers, treasurer and Admin accounts to ensure secure\r\nand structured system usage.\r\n Designed and built CRUD functionality for student records, payments, and invoices to streamline administrative\r\noperations.\r\n Integrated secure authentication and user profile management to protect sensitive financial and personal data.\r\n Created responsive dashboards for tracking payment status, outstanding fees, and transaction history across\r\ndevices.\r\n Optimized frontend performance and database queries to improve page load speed and overall user experience.\r\n\r\nAttendance tracking system: - https://youtu.be/_kAXwVKVB_g\r\n\r\n Built a Java-based attendance management system using Servlets, JSP, and MySQL.\r\n Applied DAO pattern with JDBC for clean and maintainable database access.\r\n Implemented authentication, student management, attendance tracking, and reporting features.\r\n Designed and integrated a MySQL database with structured relational tables.\r\n Deployed and tested the system on Apache Tomcat.\r\n\r\nHabit tracker (full stack) - https://youtu.be/8kXRjqR1SG4\r\n\r\n Engineered a full-stack habit tracker using Next.js, Tailwind CSS, and Supabase, enabling users to seamlessly track\r\nand manage daily routines.\r\n Designed and implemented CRUD operations for habits, reducing task management complexity and improving\r\nuser efficiency.\r\n Integrated secure authentication with password reset and profile management, enhancing account reliability and\r\ndata protection.\r\n Developed a responsive dashboard and profile pages, increasing accessibility across desktop and mobile devices.\r\n Optimized frontend performance and database queries, reducing page load time by ~18% and improving overall\r\nuser experience.\r\n\r\nSocial media Rest Api (backend)\r\n\r\n Developed a scalable REST API using Node.js, Express, and MongoDB to support user accounts, posts, and\r\ncomments for a social media platform.\r\n Implemented JWT-based authentication and authorization middleware, strengthening route security and\r\nsafeguarding user data.\r\n Designed optimized Mongoose schemas and relationships, improving query performance and ensuring data\r\nconsistency across collections.\r\n Built custom middleware for error handling, validation, and access control, reducing runtime errors by ~22%\r\nduring testing.\r\n Conducted extensive API testing with Postman, ensuring reliability and consistency across endpoints.\r\n Leveraged MongoDB Compass for efficient data modeling, monitoring, and database management.\r\n\r\nDiabetes prediction machine learning project (full stack) - https://youtu.be/XTBJwLbrtDM\r\n\r\n Developed a full-stack diabetes prediction platform with a Next.js frontend and FastAPI backend, enabling real-\r\ntime health predictions.\r\n Trained a Random Forest model on the Pima Indians Diabetes dataset, achieving reliable classification of\r\ndiabetes risk based on 8 health indicators. Designed an interactive form for user input and dynamically displayed personalized predictions, medicines, and\r\nhealth tips.\r\n Implemented CORS-enabled backend services, ensuring seamless communication between frontend and\r\nbackend.\r\n Optimized data handling and model integration, reducing API response time by ~20% and improving user\r\nexperience.\r\n\r\nBiteTok (full stack) - https://youtu.be/s6hQT9V_t0k\r\n\r\n Built a full-stack web application that combines TikTok-style short videos with a food ordering system, enhancing\r\nuser engagement with interactive content.\r\n Developed the frontend with HTML, Tailwind CSS, and JavaScript, delivering a responsive interface across mobile\r\nand desktop devices.\r\n Implemented a PHP backend to manage video uploads, order processing, and data storage, ensuring smooth\r\nplatform operations.\r\n Integrated video upload, playback, search, and filtering features, improving discoverability and usability for users.\r\n Designed a modern, responsive UI/UX, increasing accessibility and user retention.\r\n\r\nLost and found assistant (full stack) - https://youtu.be/PL2GQMPpMUQ\r\n\r\n Developed a full-stack web application that allows users to submit, search, and claim lost or found items,\r\nstreamlining item recovery.\r\n Built a responsive admin dashboard for item management, reporting, and oversight, improving platform\r\norganization and efficiency.\r\n Implemented secure user authentication and access control, ensuring safe login/registration and data protection.\r\n Designed and integrated search and filter features, making item discovery faster and more accurate.\r\n Created backend APIs in PHP for database interaction and file uploads, leveraging MySQL for structured data\r\nstorage.\r\n Designed a consistent HTML/CSS interface styled with Bootstrap, delivering a professional and user-friendly\r\nexperience.\r\n\r\nbank-account-management (java oop) - https://youtu.be/N1JXdY-hoa0\r\n\r\n Developed a desktop banking application in Java using Swing, enabling users to securely manage accounts and\r\ntransactions.\r\n Implemented user login authentication and security features, protecting sensitive financial data.\r\n Built core banking functions including account balance tracking, deposits, withdrawals, and transaction history.\r\n Utilized file handling with .dat files to store user and transaction records, ensuring persistent and reliable data\r\nstorage.\r\n Applied object-oriented programming principles to deliver scalable, maintainable, and modular code.\r\n Designed a user-friendly interface with error handling, enhancing usability and reducing user input errors.\r\n Collaborated in a team setting to extend functionality and improve application performance.\r\n\r\nTic-Tac-Toe:\r\n\r\n Designed and implemented a complete Tic-Tac-Toe game engine by applying core object-oriented programming\r\n(OOP) principles, resulting in a well-structured and scalable codebase.\r\n Architected the solution using classes for the game board and players with encapsulation and inheritance, which\r\nenhanced code organization and simplified debugging and testing processes.\r\n Engineered the core game logic, including turn management, win-state validation, and draw\r\nconditions, ensuring a flawless and deterministic user experience. Developed an interactive command-line interface with robust input validation and replay functionality, leading\r\nto a user-friendly and error-resistant application.\r\n Wrote clean, modular, and thoroughly commented code to promote maintainability and ease of future feature\r\nintegration, demonstrating strong software engineering best practices.\r\n\r\nOnline Food Ordering System (C++ - DSA Project):\r\n\r\n Architected a console-based food ordering system by implementing core data structures (singly-linked lists,\r\nqueues) to model dynamic order management and a FIFO processing pipeline, efficiently handling real-world\r\noperational flows.\r\n Engineered efficient algorithms for menu operations, utilizing merge sort (O(m log m)) for organization and linear\r\nsearch (O(n)) for item retrieval, optimizing the backend for performance and scalability.\r\n Designed and integrated a robust exception handling framework to manage input validation and edge\r\ncases, ensuring system stability and reliability under unpredictable user input.\r\n Achieved optimal time complexity for core functions: O(1) for enqueue/dequeue operations, O(n*m) for order\r\nmanagement, demonstrating a strong command of computational efficiency.\r\n Validated system integrity through extensive unit and integration testing, resulting in a robust, error-tolerant\r\napplication ready for demonstration.\r\n\r\nREFERENCES\r\n\r\n Dr. Zatul Alwani Shaffiei\r\n Software Engineering Program Coordinator,\r\n Malaysia–Japan International Institute of Technology (MJIIT)\r\n Universiti Teknologi Malaysia, Kuala Lumpur\r\n Email: zatulalwani.kl@utm.my\r\n Phone No: +6013-6849664\r\n	{"title":"resume","summary_steps":"This is a resume for Muntasir Rahaman Sirkhazi, a software engineering student.","key_points":"• Muntasir Rahaman Sirkhazi is a software engineering student with expertise in full-stack development.\\n• He is currently pursuing a Bachelor of Computer Science at Malaysia–Japan International Institute of Technology (MJIIT), University Technology Malaysia.\\n• His hard skills include MySQL, PHP, HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Python, Java, C++, React.js, Node.js, Next.js, and MongoDB.\\n• He has developed several full-stack projects including a Smart Interview Analyzer, Payment Tracking System, and Habit Tracker.\\n• Projects also include a Social Media REST API, Diabetes Prediction Machine Learning project, and BiteTok.\\n• He has experience with Java OOP projects like a Bank Account Management application and an Attendance Tracking System.","sop":"Document Type / Title\\n• resume\\n\\nName / Author\\n• MUNTASIR RAHAMAN SIRKHAZI\\n\\nContact Information\\n• Malaysia, Kuala Lumpur\\n• muntasirrahman23@gmail.com\\n• 010 707 6149\\n• github\\n• Linkedin\\n\\nEducation\\n• Bachelor of Computer Science (Software Engineering) with Honours, Malaysia–Japan International Institute of Technology (MJIIT), UNIVERSITY TECHNOLOGY MALAYSIA, October, 2023 (CURRENT)\\n• Senior Secondary School (STPM/A-Levels Equivalent), INTERNATIONAL INDIAN SCHOOL DAMMAM, SAUDI ARABIA, April, 2020 - April, 2021\\n• Secondary School (SPM/O-Levels Equivalent), INTERNATIONAL INDIAN SCHOOL DAMMAM, SAUDI ARABIA, April, 2018 - April, 2019\\n\\nSkills\\n• MySQL\\n• php\\n• html\\n• CSS\\n• JAVASCRIPT\\n• python\\n• Java\\n• C++\\n• React js\\n• bootstrap\\n• tailwind css\\n• Assembly Language\\n• node.js\\n• nextjs\\n• mongo db\\n• Communication\\n• Teamwork\\n• Problem-solving\\n• Adaptability\\n• Time management\\n• Leadership\\n• Creativity\\n\\nTools / Technologies\\n• GitHub\\n• Cisco Packet Tracer\\n• postman\\n• Microsoft VScode\\n• Oracle VirtualBox\\n• Geekbench\\n• CPU-Z\\n• mongodb\\n• Tampermonkey\\n\\nProjects / Work Experience\\n• Smart Interview Analyzer: full-stack asynchronous media analysis platform using React + Tailwind, Node.js (Express), Python, and PostgreSQL\\n• Payment Tracking System (full stack): tuition payment management system using Next.js, Tailwind CSS, and Supabase for a private tuition center\\n• Attendance tracking system: Java-based attendance management system using Servlets, JSP, and MySQL\\n• Habit tracker (full stack): habit tracker using Next.js, Tailwind CSS, and Supabase\\n• Social media Rest Api (backend): scalable REST API using Node.js, Express, and MongoDB\\n• Diabetes prediction machine learning project (full stack): diabetes prediction platform with a Next.js frontend and FastAPI backend\\n• BiteTok (full stack): web application combining TikTok-style short videos with a food ordering system\\n• Lost and found assistant (full stack): web application for submitting, searching, and claiming lost or found items\\n• bank-account-management (java oop): desktop banking application in Java using Swing\\n• Tic-Tac-Toe: complete Tic-Tac-Toe game engine applying core object-oriented programming\\n\\nOther Relevant Information\\n• Languages: English, Hindi and Urdu","